cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Market consolidation and network redundancy in Ukraine's
  fixed-line ISP sector, 2021-2026
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Atanasov
    given-names: Vitalii
    city: Kyiv
    country: UA
abstract: >-
  Routing-data analysis of Ukraine's fixed-line internet
  provider market before and after the October 2024
  withdrawal of the simplified tax regime for small
  providers. Combines RIPEstat autonomous-system series,
  PeeringDB network classification, and prefix-level
  substitution analysis to measure how much of the market
  is observable in routing data at all. Separates market
  consolidation from the appropriation of networks in
  occupied territory.
keywords:
  - internet infrastructure
  - network resilience
  - BGP
  - Ukraine
  - telecommunications regulation
  - market consolidation
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-08'
